  "id": "RLSA-2026:58936",
  "title": "Important: sqlite security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-08-25 18:04:05"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-09-03 00:12:51"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "SQLite is a C library that implements an SQL database engine. A large subset of SQL92 is supported. A complete database is stored in a single disk file. The API is designed for convenience and ease of use. Applications that link against SQLite can enjoy the power and flexibility of an SQL database without the administrative hassles of supporting a separate database server.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* sqlite: SQLite: Arbitrary code execution via crafted FTS5 full-text search data (CVE-2026-11822)\n\n* sqlite: SQLite: Arbitrary code execution and crash via heap-based buffer overflow in FTS5 (CVE-2026-11824)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
